Z||000000||camaro2fiero||05-24-2001||09:06 PM||||what is the purpose of the label on the drivers side inner wheel well. It says service parts identifaction do not remove?what can I do with the info provided.||||reg||1
Z||000001||FieroJoe||05-24-2001||09:10 PM||||Is this actually <I>in</I> the wheel well, like on the splash sheild somewhere, or are you looking at the label on the backside of the wheel well, under the front hood?  If you're looking at the one that is in the front compartment, that is the RPO code sheet.  It lets people doing service work know what options are on your car.  It also has the paint code at the bottom of it.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/joesig_1.jpg"> <BR>'87 Coupe 5spd.<BR>AIM:FieroJoe87||||reg||1
Z||000002||camaro2fiero||05-24-2001||09:16 PM||||Oh Thank You FieroJoe,I was taking pictures of thecar to put on forum.They did not come out to good cause of lighting.I took pics under trees and it looks terrible.I was looking at the codes .I did not know what they were used for.One of the codes is WS8,is that for stock suspension?||||reg||1
